e original PUT at ballot 0 before recovery; the original leader reaches COMMITTED using a matching reply from a distinct installing participant.","The recovering nonleader initially has nil clientProposals and fresh bookkeeping counters.","Any delayed traffic and scheduled execution must respect stream decoding order, local mutex ownership, successful sends and actual handler prerequisites."],"excluded":["Durable restart guarantees","Client-proposal replacement during recovery","General quorum correctness across other configurations","Duplicate-response accounting","A claim of application divergence based only on an F3 assignment mismatch","Treating normal commit broadcast as correctly encoded CommitShort traffic"],"parameters":{"replica_count":3,"failure_parameter":1,"instance":0,"original_leader":0,"recovering_replica":1,"original_command":{"operation":"PUT","key":0,"value":[1]}}},"source":"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254","README.md:1:86"],"pending":["Reach the original supported decision and recovery assignment in one legal correlated execution.","Establish executable correspondence for the assignment checker and preserve original command contents independently of mutable instance objects.","Validate the transport and scheduling abstraction against actual behavior before interpreting any model counterexample as implementation evidence."],"assessment":"unassessed","candidate":true,"grounding":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"expectation_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","state/state.go:101:254"],"binding_ids":["L_recovery_assignment","L_recovery_entry","L_assignment_broadcast","L_accept_installation","L_decision_transition","L_execution_consumer"],"derivation":"The README identifies this selected implementation as classic Paxos within a replication repository; that label alone does not establish applicability. The concrete local relation supplies the principal basis: bcastAccept publishes the threshold-selected lb.cmds for the same instance, handleAcceptReply promotes the local instance to COMMITTED without comparing it with an earlier decision, and executeCommands consumes that instance as part of a monotonically advancing execution prefix. Command.Execute makes PUT state-changing, whereas NOOP contains NONE. These producers and consumers require recovery to retain an already decided instance's commands if the same instance is to remain a consistent replicated execution position. The requirement is an explicit audit inference from that relation, not an assertion that the observed overwrite is correct or that every previously accepted value must always be retained. Its premise requires a prior actual supported decision, not merely an acceptance, a counter value or the F3 fact itself.","applicability":"The constructor enables execution; the run loop dispatches recovery without an IsLeader restriction; recover supplies nil clientProposals when creating bookkeeping; and the prepare-reply threshold branch assigns NOOP in that case. The scoped N=3, F=1 configuration gives read and write thresholds of two. Thus the recovery assignment is directly consumed by this implementation's decision and execution paths under a concrete available configuration.","unresolved":["A legal schedule reaching all premises and the assignment has not been executed.","The repository does not supply an explicit standalone decision-preservation contract in the attached README; the producer-consumer derivation requires semantic review.","The implementation's concurrent shared-state accesses and transport behavior require calibration of any model abstraction."],"conflicts":["The prepare-reply handler records returned accepted commands and then unconditionally replaces lb.cmds at the threshold. Its comment explicitly notices the overwrite, but supplies no alternative semantic contract.","Normal commit broadcast uses a full Commit payload under commitShortRPC; protective commit delivery cannot be assumed to have the intended short-message semantics."],"alternatives":["A committed participant's full Commit response or a delivered commit may prevent the proposed recovery history; retain these paths in the check.","If startup, transport blocking or another reachable guard prevents the assignment under the stated premises, the candidate schedule fails without establishing overall correctness."]},"version":1}],"claims":[],"bindings":[{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"rationale":"Direct checked assignment: selects returned value information, then replaces commands with local proposals or NOOP when the preparation threshold is reached."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:539:666","start_line":539,"end_line":539,"symbol":"Replica.handlePrepareReply"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:539:666","id":"L_recovery_assignment","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.handlePrepareReply","start_line":539,"end_line":617,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"F3 establishment and outgoing acceptance initiation.","pending":["Distinct response provenance and legal invocation must be established by the execution history."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"rationale":"Direct recovery entry creates the nil-client bookkeeping that selects the checked NOOP branch."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:667:736","start_line":667,"end_line":667,"symbol":"Replica.recover"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:667:736","id":"L_recovery_entry","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.recover","start_line":667,"end_line":684,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"Initializes recovery bookkeeping and initiates preparation.","pending":["Use the actual timer enqueue and run-loop dispatch rather than assuming recovery invocation."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397"],"rationale":"Direct consumer publishes the checked assignment as Accept commands for the same instance and attempt."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:261:397","start_line":295,"end_line":295,"symbol":"Replica.bcastAccept"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:261:397","id":"L_assignment_broadcast","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.bcastAccept","start_line":295,"end_line":321,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"Reads lb.cmds and lastTriedBallot and sends to eligible peers.","pending":["Alive filtering, peer order, serialization and send completion do not themselves establish delivery."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"rationale":"Directly identifies actual acceptance installations needed for the prior-decision premise and for any subsequent consequence."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:398:538","start_line":441,"end_line":441,"symbol":"Replica.handleAccept"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:398:538","id":"L_accept_installation","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.handleAccept","start_line":441,"end_line":478,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"Distinguishes command installation from rejection and committed-instance preservation.","pending":["A matching ballot-only reply is insufficient evidence of installation without its correlated handler branch."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"rationale":"Directly locates the original decision transition whose command contents constrain recovery, and the possible later conflicting transition."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:539:666","start_line":619,"end_line":619,"symbol":"Replica.handleAcceptReply"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:539:666","id":"L_decision_transition","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.handleAcceptReply","start_line":619,"end_line":665,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"Promotes an instance to COMMITTED after matching-reply accounting and calls commit broadcast.","pending":["Record distinct participants and actual installed commands independently of the reply counter.","A second decision is a consequence witness, not a prerequisite for observing an assignment violation."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"rationale":"Direct consumer establishes why a decided instance's commands matter and supplies the actual recovery trigger."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:667:736","start_line":686,"end_line":686,"symbol":"Replica.executeCommands"},"material_id":"paxos/paxos.go:667:736","id":"L_execution_consumer","file":"paxos/paxos.go","symbol":"Replica.executeCommands","start_line":686,"end_line":736,"snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","basis":"agent_inference","description":"Consumes committed commands in prefix order and queues recovery after repeated execution-gap observations.","pending":["Actual application divergence requires correlated execution effects and prefix observations, not just differing command assignments.","The loop's timeout is incremented per observation rather than computed from elapsed wall-clock time."],"version":1,"excerpt_source":"See supplied material at the exact file and behavior range"}],"relations":[],"units":[],"open_issues":[{"conditions":[{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/1","text":"The README supplies protocol orientation, not an explicit standalone contract requiring command equality at this internal assignment.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/2","text":"A COMMITTED participant responds to Prepare with a full Commit; handleAccept preserves committed instances and rejects lower ballots. These mechanisms can prevent a particular conflicting history.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/3","text":"The assignment requirement is stronger than final agreement in an implementation that reliably filters conflicting assignments downstream. No such reliable command-comparison filter is shown here, but the supplied protective paths must still be assessed.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/4","text":"handlePrepareReply visibly overwrites selected commands, and its comment notices that behavior. Neither the overwrite nor the comment establishes an alternative intended guarantee.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/5","text":"Applicability is provisional within the explicitly selected configuration and fault scope.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/6","text":"No executed history establishes that the earlier supported decision and the recovery assignment occur together.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/7","text":"An assignment mismatch alone does not establish conflicting decisions or application divergence.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]}],"id":"29a1a2fa1d2f4524bc25f160938a964b","review_id":"98072f5807e84fc1baea13216ac40e8c","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","target_version":1,"aspect":"applicability","source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"explanation":"The responsibility has a concrete producer-consumer basis beyond the README's classic-Paxos label. handlePrepareReply assigns recovery commands to both bookkeeping and the instance, marks the instance ACCEPTED, and immediately invokes bcastAccept. handleAcceptReply subsequently commits the instance without comparing its commands with an earlier decision, and executeCommands consumes committed commands at a monotonically advancing instance position. PUT changes the store; the NONE command returned by NOOP does not perform the same operation. Preserving an independently established decision is therefore an applicable inferred responsibility for this recovery assignment. The constructor enables execution, the run loop dispatches recovery without requiring leadership, and recover creates nil-client bookkeeping for the scoped nonleader. Read and write thresholds are both two at N=3, F=1. Requiring actual distinct-participant installation support and a COMMITTED transition appropriately distinguishes the premise from an arbitrary accepted value or a reply counter.","disposition":"blocked","reason":"No actionable follow-up was supplied; the issue remains unresolved and requires planning"},{"conditions":[{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/1","text":"Full Commit responses and committed-instance acceptance protection offer alternative ways to stop a conflicting continuation; they do not guarantee preservation of the earlier assignment.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/2","text":"The prepare-threshold branch does not update vbal. A model must not silently repair that field or equate it with bal.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/3","text":"handlePrepareReply has no committed-status guard and does not reset its counters after threshold passage. Later authentic replies cannot automatically be modeled as inert merely because the immediate check focuses on the first recovery assignment.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/4","text":"Preserving every previously accepted value would be a stronger, unsupported requirement; the present obligation appropriately requires an earlier supported decision.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/5","text":"No formal predicate or executable monitor was supplied, so command equality, temporal ordering, participant identity, and antecedent reachability have not received checker-correspondence review.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/6","text":"The immediate obligation does not cover duplicate accounting, durable restart, or client-proposal replacement.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"ebe3ffd8bf554fbda1021081b80d70bd/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/7","text":"Future checks must retain the earlier decision independently and distinguish assignment, second commitment, and application effects.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]}],"id":"c4ed42142ebb4a1590982d8aaa1f5acf","review_id":"98072f5807e84fc1baea13216ac40e8c","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","target_version":1,"aspect":"decomposition","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"explanation":"The obligation isolates a meaningful preservation boundary: a previously supported decision constrains the commands selected for renewed acceptance at the same instance. The bindings cover recovery bookkeeping, threshold assignment, publication, actual acceptance installation, commitment, and ordered execution. A deep command-content snapshot of the earlier decision is necessary because recovery replaces mutable instance fields. Distinct acceptance witnesses are also necessary because AcceptReply contains only instance and ballot, and handleAccept sends a reply even when it does not install the incoming commands. Preserving this assignment is sufficient only for the stated local responsibility. The broader bad outcome could still occur while this obligation holds, through other command replacement paths, unsound reply accounting, or commit handling outside the checked assignment. Conversely, full-commit delivery or rejection can prevent a second decision despite an assignment mismatch. The claim and unit correctly retain separate consequence witnesses instead of treating this obligation as sufficient for overall agreement.","disposition":"blocked","reason":"No actionable follow-up was supplied; the issue remains unresolved and requires planning"},{"conditions":[{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/1","text":"The README identifies classic Paxos but does not explicitly specify command equality at this internal assignment; the expectation remains an attributed producer-consumer inference.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/2","text":"A committed participant answers Prepare with full Commit information. handleAccept protects committed instances and rejects lower ballots, potentially preventing a conflicting continuation.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/3","text":"Assignment preservation is stronger than final agreement where downstream mechanisms reliably suppress conflicting proposals. The supplied code shows protective branches but does not establish such reliable suppression for this scenario.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/4","text":"The overwrite comment acknowledges behavior without establishing an alternative intended guarantee.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/5","text":"bcastCommit sends a Commit object under commitShortRPC. Intended short-commit delivery semantics cannot be assumed from this call.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/6","text":"No executed history establishes the original supported decision followed by the recovery assignment.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/7","text":"Deployment, startup and scheduling assumptions remain scenario premises.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/8","text":"An assignment mismatch alone would not establish a second decision or application divergence.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/applicability/condition/9","text":"The existing applicability issue and its conditions remain unresolved.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]}],"id":"b9819fc369d547bf95b83c3943cd0418","review_id":"719aa224e92547fd87cbcc778ed3b1ec","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","target_version":1,"aspect":"applicability","source_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"explanation":"The obligation has an explicit, scoped producer-consumer justification beyond protocol naming. The recovery threshold writes both lb.cmds and inst.cmds, marks the instance ACCEPTED, and publishes those commands through bcastAccept. Matching acceptance replies can then commit that instance without checking its contents against an earlier decision; executeCommands consumes its commands at the corresponding execution position. PUT and NOOP have different state effects. Preserving an independently supported decision at this publication boundary is therefore a reasonable inferred implementation responsibility, rather than a requirement to preserve every accepted proposal. The constructor enables execution, the run loop dispatches recovery without a leadership guard, and recovery creates nil-client bookkeeping when the nonleader has none. At N=3 and F=1, both relevant thresholds are two. These sources support applicability under the declared premises, but do not establish that those premises and the assignment occur in one legal execution.","disposition":"reading","reason":"Follow-up evidence or semantic review is required","task_ids":["253b9e7057a24a6f8734a675f84bbed4"]},{"conditions":[{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/1","text":"Full Commit responses and committed-instance acceptance protection can stop a continuation without establishing preservation at the assignment itself.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/2","text":"The prepare-threshold branch leaves vbal unchanged; behavior must not silently equate it with bal.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/3","text":"handlePrepareReply has no committed-status guard and does not reset prepareOKs after threshold passage. Later authentic replies can trigger further assignments.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/4","text":"recover does not recheck committed status before preparing, so a queued recovery request cannot automatically be discarded when commit information arrives.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/5","text":"Preserving every previously accepted value would impose a stronger requirement than the supported-decision premise.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/6","text":"No formal checker or executable monitor was supplied; temporal ordering, command equality, participant identity and antecedent reachability remain unchecked.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/7","text":"Transport decoding, send blocking and local mutex constraints must be retained when investigating the correlated history.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/8","text":"Duplicate accounting, durable restart and client-proposal replacement remain outside this immediate responsibility.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]},{"id":"c9786432a2dd42d4b1a953b4d716efab/O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands/decomposition/condition/9","text":"The existing decomposition issue and its conditions remain unresolved.","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"]}],"id":"abd5d7a737c9447ea3cc3c526333fadc","review_id":"719aa224e92547fd87cbcc778ed3b1ec","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","target_version":1,"aspect":"decomposition","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"explanation":"The decomposition correctly separates the prior supported decision, recovery assignment, subsequent commitment and application. An independently retained snapshot must include ordered command contents and value bytes because recovery replaces mutable instance fields. Distinct installation witnesses are necessary: handleAccept replies even on branches that reject or preserve an existing instance, so a matching ballot or counter alone does not establish acceptance of the proposed commands. The selected bindings cover bookkeeping creation, assignment, publication, installation, decision and execution consumption. Satisfying this obligation excludes replacement at the selected recovery boundary only. Broader disagreement could still arise through other command replacement paths, reply accounting or commit processing while this obligation holds. Conversely, commit information or acceptance rejection could prevent a conflicting decision after an assignment mismatch. The narrower obligation and separate consequence witnesses therefore remain appropriate.","disposition":"reading","reason":"Follow-up evidence or semantic review is required","task_ids":["253b9e7057a24a6f8734a675f84bbed4"]}],"blocked_review_tasks":[],"overview_limit":"This compact index is not complete implementation coverage; request specific actual ranges before deriving new claims","selected_unit":{"id":"unit-O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","obligation_ids":["O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands"],"binding_ids":["L_recovery_assignment","L_recovery_entry","L_assignment_broadcast","L_accept_installation","L_decision_transition","L_execution_consumer"],"relation_ids":[],"scope":{"description":"F3 establishment during recovery of instance 0 at a nonleader after an original leader has decided a singleton PUT. Check the recovery assignment against the earlier decision's recorded command contents; assess subsequent conflicting commitment and application as separate consequences.","assumptions":["Three distinct replicas run in separate processes with IDs 0, 1 and 2, N=3 and F=1.","The master explicitly selects replica 0 as the initial leader; no leadership or membership change occurs during the checked prefix.","Startup, peer connections and initial proposal admission complete successfully.","Exec=true, Dreply=true, Durable=false and the latency configuration is empty.","Messages are authentic repository-generated messages; no duplicate replies, crashes or restarts occur.","Both nonleaders actually install the original PUT at ballot 0 before recovery; the original leader reaches COMMITTED using a matching reply from a distinct installing participant.","The recovering nonleader initially has nil clientProposals and fresh bookkeeping counters.","Any delayed traffic and scheduled execution must respect stream decoding order, local mutex ownership, successful sends and actual handler prerequisites."],"excluded":["Durable restart guarantees","Client-proposal replacement during recovery","General quorum correctness across other configurations","Duplicate-response accounting","A claim of application divergence based only on an F3 assignment mismatch","Treating normal commit broadcast as correctly encoded CommitShort traffic"],"parameters":{"replica_count":3,"failure_parameter":1,"instance":0,"original_leader":0,"recovering_replica":1,"original_command":{"operation":"PUT","key":0,"value":[1]}}},"rationale":"Continue the same F3 establishment candidate. Source review now supports one bounded obligation without another repository read: preserve the earlier supported decision's command sequence at the recovery assignment consumed by bcastAccept. Compare the assignment with independently retained prior-decision contents, rather than assuming the property in model behavior. The normal commit serialization mismatch and full-commit protection remain active counterarguments. An assignment counterexample would establish only the scoped model result until an actual legal correlated trace confirms it; conflicting decisions and application divergence require separate consequence witnesses.","status":"blocked","previous_id":null,"version":1,"boundary_changes":[],"obligation_checks":{},"remaining_obligation_ids":["O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands"],"recheck_reasons":[],"semantic_readiness":{"unit_version":1,"target_versions":{"unit-O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands":1,"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands":1},"material_ids":["README.md:1:86","master/master.go:1:200","master/master.go:201:277","paxos/defs.go:181:558","paxos/defs.go:1:180","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:1:23","paxos/paxos.go:237:267","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/defs/latency.go:1:238","replica/replica.go:137:340","replica/replica.go:1:80","replica/replica.go:341:577","replica/replica.go:81:136","run.go:23:103","state/state.go:101:254","state/state.go:1:100"],"review_ids":["719aa224e92547fd87cbcc778ed3b1ec","98072f5807e84fc1baea13216ac40e8c"],"status":"disputed","unresolved":["unit-O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands:decomposition","O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands:decomposition","O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands:applicability","29a1a2fa1d2f4524bc25f160938a964b","c4ed42142ebb4a1590982d8aaa1f5acf","f1cb9e8a38bb4803a52502ebd532bc56","b9819fc369d547bf95b83c3943cd0418","abd5d7a737c9447ea3cc3c526333fadc"],"purpose":"Continue the same F3 establishment candidate. Source review now supports one bounded obligation without another repository read: preserve the earlier supported decision's command sequence at the recovery assignment consumed by bcastAccept. Compare the assignment with independently retained prior-decision contents, rather than assuming the property in model behavior. The normal commit serialization mismatch and full-commit protection remain active counterarguments. An assignment counterexample would establish only the scoped model result until an actual legal correlated trace confirms it; conflicting decisions and application divergence require separate consequence witnesses.","limitation":"Exploratory checking is allowed; unreviewed or disputed semantics cannot confirm implementation defects"},"audit_question":{"disposition":"ready_for_check","preferred_check":"local_model","requests":[],"question":"When F3 is established during recovery without client proposals, can a replica replace commands from an earlier supported decision with NOOP and subsequently obtain a conflicting decision before protective commit information arrives?","importance":"The assignment feeds acceptance, commitment and ordered application without a later comparison against an earlier decision. A reachable replacement could therefore lead to different commands occupying the same replicated execution position. The assignment obligation and the broader consequences require separate witnesses.","source_ids":["README.md:1:86","run.go:23:103","master/master.go:1:200","master/master.go:201:277","paxos/paxos.go:1:23","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:237:267","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","paxos/defs.go:1:180","paxos/defs.go:181:558","replica/replica.go:1:80","replica/replica.go:81:136","replica/replica.go:137:340","replica/replica.go:341:577","replica/defs/latency.go:1:238","state/state.go:1:100","state/state.go:101:254"],"participants":["Original leader replica 0","Recovering nonleader replica 1","Nonleader replica 2 retaining the original acceptance","Master registration service","Per-peer listeners and message-dispatch goroutines","Replica run and execution goroutines"],"objects":["F3 assignment for instance 0","Recorded original decision command contents","Instance commands, bal, vbal and status","Recovery bookkeeping and reply counters","Actual acceptance installations and distinct participants","Full Commit and CommitShort wire representations","Peer streams, dispatch queues and local send mutexes","Application state and execution prefix"],"contexts":["Fresh separate processes; N=3, F=1, Exec=true, Dreply=true, Durable=false.","Distinct endpoint registrations assign IDs 0, 1 and 2; explicit master leader configuration selects replica 0.","Startup, IP lookup, endpoint probing, peer setup and beacon phase complete successfully.","Empty latency configuration; finite scheduling and transport delays remain possible.","Both nonleaders install the singleton PUT at ballot 0 before replica 0 reaches its decision threshold.","Replica 1 recovers with nil clientProposals and fresh counters; replica 2 remains available to process recovery exchanges.","No crashes, restarts, duplicate replies, membership changes or leader changes occur in the checked prefix.","Protective leader traffic is delayed only through a schedule that respects actual streams, mutexes and handler prerequisites."],"event_paths":["Complete startup -> replica 0 admits singleton PUT at instance 0 -> complete its initial prepare path -> both nonleaders install Accept at ballot 0 -> replica 0 processes a matching reply and records COMMITTED with PUT -> preserve an independent snapshot of that decision -> delay protective leader traffic -> replica 1 accumulates execution-gap observations and dispatches recover -> replica 2 answers ballot-1 Prepare with its retained ballot-0 PUT -> replica 1 reaches F3 and compare assigned commands with the original decision -> separately explore NOOP acceptance, a second COMMITTED transition and application effects."],"activity_classes":["A1","A2","A3","A5"],"behavior_ids":["B2","B3","B4","B5","B8"],"fact_ids":["F3"],"obligation_relation_kind":"establishment","counterevidence":["A COMMITTED instance answers Prepare with a full Commit under commitRPC, using inst.vbal and retained commands. This protective path must remain present.","handleAccept preserves COMMITTED instances and rejects incoming ballots below the promise.","PrepareReply and AcceptReply handlers compare reply ballots with lastTriedBallot; stale or higher-ballot replies cannot be treated as matching support.","Both thresholds equal two for the scoped configuration. The history requires distinct participants and actual installation branches, not duplicated counters or rejection replies.","A nonleader's makeBallot uses its replica ID. Leader 0 followed by recovering replica 1 is a substantive ballot premise.","SendMsg holds M during serialization and Flush; blocked sends may prevent recovery progress or execution-loop lock acquisition.","Peer streams decode sequentially. Per-message dispatch goroutines do not permit unread bytes to bypass preceding bytes on the same stream.","Broadcasts depend on Alive peers and usable writers; listener errors or unknown message types can obstruct the candidate history.","Normal bcastCommit pairs Commit.Marshal with commitShortRPC. For one PUT at key 0, the short decoder interprets payload bytes 12–15 as ballot 258; remaining command bytes remain in the stream. This source-derived decoding result is not an observed execution and cannot be replaced with intended short-commit semantics.","The original leader's prepare-threshold branch does not update vbal. A later full Commit response can therefore carry a ballot different from inst.bal and may be rejected by a higher-promise receiver.","F3 alone establishes only a local assignment; neither a second decision nor application divergence follows without additional correlated observations.","README protocol naming supports orientation but does not independently establish the obligation; the stated expectation depends on the explicit producer-consumer derivation."],"unknowns":["Whether one legal correlated execution reaches startup, original support, the original COMMITTED transition, timer-driven recovery and the F3 assignment while preserving all applicable protections.","Whether the actual transport and scheduler permit the required finite delay of leader-originated traffic without blocking the nonleaders' exchanges or causing earlier stream failure.","Whether a second supported decision occurs after the assignment, and whether different application effects occur in that same history.","Whether a proposed model correctly represents local self contribution, unchanged vbal fields, reply counters, protected commit branches and malformed commit traffic.","No executable trace, calibrated model or supported monitor has established the proposed outcome.","The master parameters and registration order are selected scenario premises, not observations of a deployed configuration.","Successful constructor IP lookup, endpoint probing and startup remain experiment prerequisites.","Durable restart and client-proposal replacement variants remain outside this immediate check.","The inferred decision-preservation requirement still requires semantic applicability and checker-correspondence review."],"priority":1,"trigger_rationale":"The latest sources resolve the remaining immediate code gaps. PUT changes the key-value store; NOOP contains NONE, which does not mutate it and is skipped by the nonclient PUT-only execution branch. Command encoding determines the malformed commit header rather than leaving its bytes hypothetical. The execution loop increments timeout by 1,000,000 per observation and enqueues recovery at 3,000,000,000, requiring 3,000 gap observations for the initial instance-0 gap, with a one-millisecond sleep on nonexecuting iterations; this is not a strict wall-clock deadline. A local producer-consumer requirement and an independent command-equality oracle are now available. Use a bounded model to explore the coupled legal histories, retaining transport protections and requiring executable calibration before implementation conclusions."},"coverage_limitations":[]},"semantic_view":{"issue_reference_rule":"explanation_ref/source_ids_ref point to the exact unchanged fields of open_issues by issue ID; all alternatives and counterarguments remain on the judgment","judgments":[{"review_id":"98072f5807e84fc1baea13216ac40e8c","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"aspect":"applicability","status":"no_issue_found","counterevidence":["The README supplies protocol orientation, not an explicit standalone contract requiring command equality at this internal assignment.","A COMMITTED participant responds to Prepare with a full Commit; handleAccept preserves committed instances and rejects lower ballots. These mechanisms can prevent a particular conflicting history.","The assignment requirement is stronger than final agreement in an implementation that reliably filters conflicting assignments downstream. No such reliable command-comparison filter is shown here, but the supplied protective paths must still be assessed.","handlePrepareReply visibly overwrites selected commands, and its comment notices that behavior. Neither the overwrite nor the comment establishes an alternative intended guarantee."],"limitations":["Applicability is provisional within the explicitly selected configuration and fault scope.","No executed history establishes that the earlier supported decision and the recovery assignment occur together.","An assignment mismatch alone does not establish conflicting decisions or application divergence."],"current_version":true,"issue_ref":"29a1a2fa1d2f4524bc25f160938a964b","explanation_ref":"29a1a2fa1d2f4524bc25f160938a964b","source_ids_ref":"29a1a2fa1d2f4524bc25f160938a964b"},{"review_id":"98072f5807e84fc1baea13216ac40e8c","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"aspect":"decomposition","status":"no_issue_found","counterevidence":["Full Commit responses and committed-instance acceptance protection offer alternative ways to stop a conflicting continuation; they do not guarantee preservation of the earlier assignment.","The prepare-threshold branch does not update vbal. A model must not silently repair that field or equate it with bal.","handlePrepareReply has no committed-status guard and does not reset its counters after threshold passage. Later authentic replies cannot automatically be modeled as inert merely because the immediate check focuses on the first recovery assignment.","Preserving every previously accepted value would be a stronger, unsupported requirement; the present obligation appropriately requires an earlier supported decision."],"limitations":["No formal predicate or executable monitor was supplied, so command equality, temporal ordering, participant identity, and antecedent reachability have not received checker-correspondence review.","The immediate obligation does not cover duplicate accounting, durable restart, or client-proposal replacement.","Future checks must retain the earlier decision independently and distinguish assignment, second commitment, and application effects."],"current_version":true,"issue_ref":"c4ed42142ebb4a1590982d8aaa1f5acf","explanation_ref":"c4ed42142ebb4a1590982d8aaa1f5acf","source_ids_ref":"c4ed42142ebb4a1590982d8aaa1f5acf"},{"review_id":"719aa224e92547fd87cbcc778ed3b1ec","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"aspect":"applicability","status":"no_issue_found","counterevidence":["The README identifies classic Paxos but does not explicitly specify command equality at this internal assignment; the expectation remains an attributed producer-consumer inference.","A committed participant answers Prepare with full Commit information. handleAccept protects committed instances and rejects lower ballots, potentially preventing a conflicting continuation.","Assignment preservation is stronger than final agreement where downstream mechanisms reliably suppress conflicting proposals. The supplied code shows protective branches but does not establish such reliable suppression for this scenario.","The overwrite comment acknowledges behavior without establishing an alternative intended guarantee.","bcastCommit sends a Commit object under commitShortRPC. Intended short-commit delivery semantics cannot be assumed from this call."],"limitations":["No executed history establishes the original supported decision followed by the recovery assignment.","Deployment, startup and scheduling assumptions remain scenario premises.","An assignment mismatch alone would not establish a second decision or application divergence.","The existing applicability issue and its conditions remain unresolved."],"current_version":true,"issue_ref":"b9819fc369d547bf95b83c3943cd0418","explanation_ref":"b9819fc369d547bf95b83c3943cd0418","source_ids_ref":"b9819fc369d547bf95b83c3943cd0418"},{"review_id":"719aa224e92547fd87cbcc778ed3b1ec","target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","version":1,"aspect":"decomposition","status":"no_issue_found","counterevidence":["Full Commit responses and committed-instance acceptance protection can stop a continuation without establishing preservation at the assignment itself.","The prepare-threshold branch leaves vbal unchanged; behavior must not silently equate it with bal.","handlePrepareReply has no committed-status guard and does not reset prepareOKs after threshold passage. Later authentic replies can trigger further assignments.","recover does not recheck committed status before preparing, so a queued recovery request cannot automatically be discarded when commit information arrives.","Preserving every previously accepted value would impose a stronger requirement than the supported-decision premise."],"limitations":["No formal checker or executable monitor was supplied; temporal ordering, command equality, participant identity and antecedent reachability remain unchecked.","Transport decoding, send blocking and local mutex constraints must be retained when investigating the correlated history.","Duplicate accounting, durable restart and client-proposal replacement remain outside this immediate responsibility.","The existing decomposition issue and its conditions remain unresolved."],"current_version":true,"issue_ref":"abd5d7a737c9447ea3cc3c526333fadc","explanation_ref":"abd5d7a737c9447ea3cc3c526333fadc","source_ids_ref":"abd5d7a737c9447ea3cc3c526333fadc"}],"resolved":[],"archive_access":"Request a focused review of a named issue/review to retrieve its archived reasoning; these are scoped opinions, not proof"},"required_material_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/defs.go:1:558","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:137:577","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:101:254","state/state.go:1:100"],"review_contract":[{"source_ranges":[{"file":"README.md","content_digest":"75ad43f329f505f9c674ae19c35b72c236962ad5ccc66e081809346c319b9b31","ranges":[[1,86]]},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","ranges":[[164,736]]},{"file":"replica/replica.go","content_digest":"ea28e2b94198a705e6dd9892a6154ce9b8cb424ec3dedeed8f8bd2488341e766","ranges":[[81,136]]},{"file":"state/state.go","content_digest":"58de228aef525681280999221d8cc4d8d14bf7d15b337a5179ce5697d5cba9a5","ranges":[[1,254]]}],"target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","object_type":"obligation","version":1,"required_aspects":["applicability","decomposition"],"questions":{"applicability":"Why does the implementation owe this responsibility in the selected scope?","decomposition":"Explain necessity, sufficiency, alternatives, producer/consumer dependencies and remaining guarantees."},"optional_questions":{},"required_material_ids":["README.md:1:86","paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736","replica/replica.go:81:136","state/state.go:101:254","state/state.go:1:100"],"dependency_versions":{"L_accept_installation":1,"L_assignment_broadcast":1,"L_decision_transition":1,"L_execution_consumer":1,"L_recovery_assignment":1,"L_recovery_entry":1,"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands":1}}],"required_review_pairs":[{"target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","aspect":"applicability"},{"target_id":"O_recovery_assignment_preserves_decided_commands","aspect":"decomposition"}],"file_lookup":[{"file":"README.md","lines":86,"unavailable":null},{"file":"paxos/defs.go","lines":558,"unavailable":null},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","lines":736,"unavailable":null},{"file":"replica/replica.go","lines":577,"unavailable":null},{"file":"state/state.go","lines":254,"unavailable":null}],"lookup_request":"Request a focused ReadingPlan for an unlisted path or symbol; omitted files are not absent from the repository","file_metadata":[{"file":"README.md","lines":86,"content_digest":"75ad43f329f505f9c674ae19c35b72c236962ad5ccc66e081809346c319b9b31","snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","encoding":"utf-8","read_ranges":[[1,80],[1,86]],"attached_ranges":[[1,86]]},{"file":"paxos/defs.go","lines":558,"content_digest":"87b0469761c5ac61a8ce960b1b32024750ec71509d08c45448325c9342d03f49","snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","encoding":"utf-8","read_ranges":[[1,180],[181,558],[1,558]],"attached_ranges":[[1,558]]},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","lines":736,"content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb","snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","encoding":"utf-8","read_ranges":[[24,163],[398,538],[539,666],[667,736],[24,260],[261,397],[237,267],[24,236],[1,23],[164,538]],"attached_ranges":[[398,538],[539,666],[667,736],[261,397],[24,236],[164,538]]},{"file":"replica/replica.go","lines":577,"content_digest":"ea28e2b94198a705e6dd9892a6154ce9b8cb424ec3dedeed8f8bd2488341e766","snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","encoding":"utf-8","read_ranges":[[1,80],[81,136],[137,340],[341,577],[137,577]],"attached_ranges":[[81,136],[137,577]]},{"file":"state/state.go","lines":254,"content_digest":"58de228aef525681280999221d8cc4d8d14bf7d15b337a5179ce5697d5cba9a5","snapshot_id":"13c33d800a184007b66dd1a3d28d1c2c","encoding":"utf-8","read_ranges":[[1,80],[1,100],[101,254]],"attached_ranges":[[1,100],[101,254]]}],"material_budget":{"used":{"unique_chars":70034,"unique_chunks":14},"breadth":{"unique_chars":70034,"unique_chunks":14,"total_chars":120000,"total_chunks":40,"reserved_for_other_chars":4973,"available_chars":44993,"available_chunks":14,"purpose":"breadth","allocation_reason":"Protect finite local dependency/review capacity","accounting":"Unique normalized source lines including one logical separator per line; not prompt tokens or a bill"},"depth":{"unique_chars":70034,"unique_chunks":14,"total_chars":120000,"total_chunks":40,"reserved_for_other_chars":0,"available_chars":49966,"available_chunks":26,"purpose":"depth","allocation_reason":"Protect finite breadth exploration capacity","accounting":"Unique normalized source lines including one logical separator per line; not prompt tokens or a bill"}},"remaining_agent_calls":2,"context_limit_chars":180000,"reading_status":[],"source_text_pool":[{"view_id":"source-view-3","citation_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:164:538","paxos/paxos.go:24:236","paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":24,"end_line":736,"text":"type Replica struct {\n\t*replica.Replica\n\tprepareChan           chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tacceptChan            chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tcommitChan            chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tcommitShortChan       chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tprepareReplyChan      chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tacceptReplyChan       chan fastrpc.Serializable\n\tinstancesToRecover    chan int32\n\tprepareRPC            uint8\n\tacceptRPC             uint8\n\tcommitRPC             uint8\n\tcommitShortRPC        uint8\n\tprepareReplyRPC       uint8\n\tacceptReplyRPC        uint8\n\tIsLeader              bool\n\tinstanceSpace         []*Instance\n\tcrtInstance           int32\n\tmaxRecvBallot         int32\n\tdefaultBallot         []int32\n\tsmallestDefaultBallot int32\n\tShutdown              bool\n\tcounter               int\n\tflush                 bool\n\texecutedUpTo          int32\n\tbatchWait             int\n\n\ttotalRecNum  int\n\ttotalSendNum int\n}\n\ntype InstanceStatus int\n\nconst (\n\tPREPARING InstanceStatus = iota\n\tPREPARED\n\tACCEPTED\n\tCOMMITTED\n)\n\ntype Instance struct {\n\tcmds   []state.Command\n\tbal    int32\n\tvbal   int32\n\tstatus InstanceStatus\n\tlb     *LeaderBookkeeping\n}\n\ntype LeaderBookkeeping struct {\n\tclientProposals []*defs.GPropose\n\tprepareOKs      int\n\tacceptOKs       int\n\tnacks           int\n\tballot          int32\n\tcmds            []state.Command\n\tlastTriedBallot int32\n}\n\nfunc New(alias string, id int, addrs []string, isLeader bool, f int, conf *config.Config, logger *dlog.Logger) *Replica {\n\tr := &Replica{\n\t\tReplica: replica.New(alias, id, f, addrs, false, true, false, conf, logger),\n\n\t\tprepareChan:      make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tacceptChan:       make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tcommitChan:       make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tcommitShortChan:  make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tprepareReplyChan: make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tacceptReplyChan:  make(chan fastrpc.Serializable, 3*defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\n\t\tinstancesToRecover: make(chan int32, 3*defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tinstanceSpace:      make([]*Instance, 15*1024*1024),\n\n\t\tcrtInstance:   -1,\n\t\tmaxRecvBallot: -1,\n\t\tdefaultBallot: make([]int32, len(addrs)),\n\n\t\tsmallestDefaultBallot: -1,\n\n\t\tIsLeader: isLeader,\n\n\t\tflush:        true,\n\t\texecutedUpTo: -1,\n\t}\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(r.defaultBallot); i++ {\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[i] = -1\n\t}\n\n\tr.prepareRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Prepare), r.prepareChan)\n\tr.acceptRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Accept), r.acceptChan)\n\tr.commitRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Commit), r.commitChan)\n\tr.commitShortRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(CommitShort), r.commitShortChan)\n\tr.prepareReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(PrepareReply), r.prepareReplyChan)\n\tr.acceptReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(AcceptReply), r.acceptReplyChan)\n\n\tgo r.run()\n\n\treturn r\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) recordInstanceMetadata(inst *Instance) {\n\tif !r.Durable {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tvar b [5]byte\n\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(b[0:4], uint32(inst.bal))\n\tb[4] = byte(inst.status)\n\tr.StableStore.Write(b[:])\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) recordCommands(cmds []state.Command) {\n\tif !r.Durable {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif cmds == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(cmds); i++ {\n\t\tcmds[i].Marshal(io.Writer(r.StableStore))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) sync() {\n\tif !r.Durable {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tr.StableStore.Sync()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) BeTheLeader(args *defs.BeTheLeaderArgs, reply *defs.BeTheLeaderReply) error {\n\tr.IsLeader = true\n\tr.totalRecNum = 0\n\tr.totalSendNum = 0\n\tr.Println(\"I am the leader\")\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) replyPrepare(replicaId int32, reply *PrepareReply) {\n\tr.SendMsg(replicaId, r.prepareReplyRPC, reply)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) replyAccept(replicaId int32, reply *AcceptReply) {\n\tr.SendMsg(replicaId, r.acceptReplyRPC, reply)\n}\n\nvar fastClockChan chan bool\n\nfunc (r *Replica) fastClock() {\n\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n\t\ttime.Sleep(time.Duration(r.batchWait) * time.Millisecond)\n\t\tfastClockChan <- true\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) BatchingEnabled() bool {\n\treturn r.batchWait > 0\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) run() {\n\n\tr.ConnectToPeers()\n\n\tr.ComputeClosestPeers()\n\n\tif r.Exec {\n\t\tgo r.executeCommands()\n\t}\n\n\tfastClockChan = make(chan bool, 1)\n\n\tif r.BatchingEnabled() {\n\t\tgo r.fastClock()\n\t}\n\n\tonOffProposeChan := r.ProposeChan\n\n\tgo r.WaitForClientConnections()\n\n\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase propose := <-onOffProposeChan:\n\t\t\tr.handlePropose(propose)\n\t\t\tif r.BatchingEnabled() {\n\t\t\t\tonOffProposeChan = nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase <-fastClockChan:\n\t\t\tonOffProposeChan = r.ProposeChan\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase prepareS := <-r.prepareChan:\n\t\t\tprepare := prepareS.(*Prepare)\n\t\t\tr.handlePrepare(prepare)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase acceptS := <-r.acceptChan:\n\t\t\taccept := acceptS.(*Accept)\n\t\t\tr.handleAccept(accept)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase commitS := <-r.commitChan:\n\t\t\tcommit := commitS.(*Commit)\n\t\t\tr.handleCommit(commit)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase commitS := <-r.commitShortChan:\n\t\t\tcommit := commitS.(*CommitShort)\n\t\t\tr.handleCommitShort(commit)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase prepareReplyS := <-r.prepareReplyChan:\n\t\t\tprepareReply := prepareReplyS.(*PrepareReply)\n\t\t\tr.handlePrepareReply(prepareReply)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase acceptReplyS := <-r.acceptReplyChan:\n\t\t\tacceptReply := acceptReplyS.(*AcceptReply)\n\t\t\tr.handleAcceptReply(acceptReply)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase iid := <-r.instancesToRecover:\n\t\t\tr.recover(iid)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) makeBallot(instance int32) {\n\tlb := r.instanceSpace[instance].lb\n\tn := int32(r.Id)\n\tif r.IsLeader {\n\t\tfor n < r.defaultBallot[r.Id] || n < r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\t\tn += int32(r.N)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tlb.lastTriedBallot = n\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastPrepare(instance int32) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Prepare bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\n\targs := &Prepare{r.Id, instance, r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.lastTriedBallot}\n\n\tn := r.N - 1\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.prepareRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t\tif sent >= n {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n}\n\nvar pa Accept\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastAccept(instance int32) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Accept bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\tpa.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpa.Instance = instance\n\tpa.Ballot = r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.lastTriedBallot\n\tpa.Command = r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.cmds\n\targs := &pa\n\n\tn := r.N - 1\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.acceptRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t\tif sent >= n {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n}\n\nvar pc Commit\nvar pcs CommitShort\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastCommit(instance int32, ballot int32, command []state.Command) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Commit bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\tpc.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpc.Instance = instance\n\tpc.Ballot = ballot\n\tpc.Command = command\n\n\tpcs.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpcs.Instance = instance\n\tpcs.Ballot = ballot\n\tpcs.Count = int32(len(command))\n\targs := &pc\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.commitShortRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t}\n\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handlePropose(propose *defs.GPropose) {\n\tif !r.IsLeader {\n\t\tpreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{FALSE, -1, state.NIL(), 0}\n\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(preply, propose.Reply, propose.Mutex)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tbatchSize := len(r.ProposeChan) + 1\n\n\tproposals := make([]*defs.GPropose, batchSize)\n\tcmds := make([]state.Command, batchSize)\n\tproposals[0] = propose\n\tcmds[0] = propose.Command\n\tfor i := 1; i < batchSize; i++ {\n\t\tprop := <-r.ProposeChan\n\t\tproposals[i] = prop\n\t\tcmds[i] = prop.Command\n\t}\n\n\tr.crtInstance++\n\tr.instanceSpace[r.crtInstance] = &Instance{\n\t\tnil,\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t&LeaderBookkeeping{proposals, 0, 0, 0, r.Id, nil, -1}}\n\tr.makeBallot(r.crtInstance)\n\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[r.crtInstance]\n\tlb := inst.lb\n\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id] = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\n\tif lb.lastTriedBallot != r.smallestDefaultBallot {\n\t\tr.bcastPrepare(r.crtInstance)\n\t} else {\n\t\tinst.cmds = cmds\n\t\tinst.lb.cmds = cmds\n\t\tinst.bal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.vbal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.status = ACCEPTED\n\t\tr.bcastAccept(r.crtInstance)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handlePrepare(prepare *Prepare) {\n\tif prepare.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = prepare.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[prepare.Instance]\n\tif inst == nil {\n\t\tif prepare.Instance > r.crtInstance {\n\t\t\tr.crtInstance = prepare.Instance\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[prepare.Instance] = &Instance{\n\t\t\tnil,\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t\tnil}\n\t\tinst = r.instanceSpace[prepare.Instance]\n\t}\n\n\tif inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\tvar pc Commit\n\t\tpc.LeaderId = prepare.LeaderId\n\t\tpc.Instance = prepare.Instance\n\t\tpc.Ballot = inst.vbal\n\t\tpc.Command = inst.cmds\n\t\targs := &pc\n\t\tr.SendMsg(pc.LeaderId, r.commitRPC, args)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif inst.bal > prepare.Ballot {\n\t} else if inst.bal < prepare.Ballot {\n\t\tinst.bal = prepare.Ballot\n\t\tinst.status = PREPARED\n\t\tif r.crtInstance == prepare.Instance {\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id] = prepare.Ballot\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tpreply := &PrepareReply{prepare.Instance, inst.bal, inst.vbal, r.defaultBallot[r.Id], r.Id, inst.cmds}\n\tr.replyPrepare(prepare.LeaderId, preply)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handleAccept(accept *Accept) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[accept.Instance]\n\n\tif accept.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = accept.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tif inst == nil {\n\t\tif accept.Instance > r.crtInstance {\n\t\t\tr.crtInstance = accept.Instance\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[accept.Instance] = &Instance{\n\t\t\taccept.Command,\n\t\t\taccept.Ballot,\n\t\t\taccept.Ballot,\n\t\t\tACCEPTED,\n\t\t\tnil}\n\t\tinst = r.instanceSpace[accept.Instance]\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[accept.Instance])\n\t\tr.recordCommands(accept.Command)\n\t\tr.sync()\n\t} else if accept.Ballot < inst.bal {\n\t\tdlog.Printf(\"Smaller ballot %d < %d\\n\", accept.Ballot, inst.bal)\n\t} else if inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\tdlog.Printf(\"Already committed \\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tinst.cmds = accept.Command\n\t\tinst.bal = accept.Ballot\n\t\tinst.vbal = accept.Ballot\n\t\tinst.status = ACCEPTED\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[accept.Instance])\n\t\tr.recordCommands(accept.Command)\n\t\tr.sync()\n\t}\n\n\tareply := &AcceptReply{accept.Instance, inst.bal}\n\tr.replyAccept(accept.LeaderId, areply)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handleCommit(commit *Commit) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance]\n\tif inst == nil {\n\t\tif commit.Instance > r.crtInstance {\n\t\t\tr.crtInstance = commit.Instance\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[commit.Instance] = &Instance{\n\t\t\tnil,\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t\tnil}\n\t\tinst = r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance]\n\t}\n\n\tif inst != nil && inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif commit.Ballot < inst.bal {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\t// FIXME timeout on client side?\n\tif inst.lb != nil && inst.lb.clientProposals != nil {\n\t\tfor _, p := range inst.lb.clientProposals {\n\t\t\tr.ProposeChan <- p\n\t\t}\n\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals = nil\n\t}\n\n\tinst.cmds = commit.Command\n\tinst.bal = commit.Ballot\n\tinst.vbal = commit.Ballot\n\tinst.status = COMMITTED\n\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance])\n\tr.recordCommands(commit.Command)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handleCommitShort(commit *CommitShort) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance]\n\tif inst == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif commit.Ballot < inst.bal {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tr.instanceSpace[commit.Instance].status = COMMITTED\n\tr.instanceSpace[commit.Instance].bal = commit.Ballot\n\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance])\n\tr.recordCommands(r.instanceSpace[commit.Instance].cmds)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handlePrepareReply(preply *PrepareReply) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance]\n\tlb := r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance].lb\n\n\tif preply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = preply.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.Ballot < lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.Ballot > lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\tlb.nacks++\n\t\tif lb.nacks+1 > r.N>>1 {\n\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(preply.Instance)\n\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(preply.Instance)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.VBallot > lb.ballot {\n\t\tlb.ballot = preply.VBallot\n\t\tlb.cmds = preply.Command\n\t}\n\n\tlb.prepareOKs++\n\tif r.defaultBallot[preply.AcceptorId] < preply.DefaultBallot {\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[preply.AcceptorId] = preply.DefaultBallot\n\t}\n\n\tif lb.prepareOKs < r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize() && len(preply.Command) != 0 {\n\t\tr.totalRecNum += len(preply.Command)\n\t\tr.Println(\"totalRecNum:\", r.totalRecNum)\n\t}\n\n\t// TODO: In the following we update lb.cmds,\n\t// ignoring `lb.cmds = preply.Command` executed\n\t// previously. This is strange\n\n\tif lb.prepareOKs+1 >= r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize() {\n\t\tif lb.clientProposals != nil {\n\t\t\tcmds := make([]state.Command, len(lb.clientProposals))\n\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(lb.clientProposals); i++ {\n\t\t\t\tcmds[i] = lb.clientProposals[i].Command\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tlb.cmds = cmds\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tlb.cmds = state.NOOP()\n\t\t}\n\t\tinst.cmds = lb.cmds\n\t\tinst.bal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.status = ACCEPTED\n\n\t\tm := int32(math.MaxInt32)\n\t\tcount := 0\n\t\tfor _, e := range r.defaultBallot {\n\t\t\tif e != -1 {\n\t\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t\t\tif e < m {\n\t\t\t\t\tm = e\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif count >= r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize()-1 && m > r.smallestDefaultBallot {\n\t\t\tr.smallestDefaultBallot = m\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance])\n\t\tr.sync()\n\t\tr.bcastAccept(preply.Instance)\n\t\tif len(inst.cmds) != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.totalSendNum += len(inst.cmds)\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"totalSendNum:\", r.totalSendNum)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handleAcceptReply(areply *AcceptReply) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance]\n\tlb := r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance].lb\n\n\tif areply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = areply.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tif inst.status >= COMMITTED {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif areply.Ballot < lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif areply.Ballot > lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\tlb.nacks++\n\t\tif lb.nacks+1 >= r.Replica.WriteQuorumSize() {\n\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(areply.Ballot)\n\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(areply.Instance)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tlb.acceptOKs++\n\tif lb.acceptOKs+1 >= r.Replica.WriteQuorumSize() {\n\t\tinst = r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance]\n\t\tinst.status = COMMITTED\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance])\n\t\tr.sync()\n\n\t\tr.bcastCommit(areply.Instance, inst.bal, inst.cmds)\n\t\tif lb.clientProposals != nil && !r.Dreply {\n\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(inst.cmds); i++ {\n\t\t\t\tpropreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n\t\t\t\t\tlb.clientProposals[i].CommandId,\n\t\t\t\t\tstate.NIL(),\n\t\t\t\t\tlb.clientProposals[i].Timestamp}\n\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(propreply, lb.clientProposals[i].Reply, lb.clientProposals[i].Mutex)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) recover(instance int32) {\n\tif r.instanceSpace[instance] == nil {\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[instance] = &Instance{\n\t\t\tnil,\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t\tnil}\n\n\t}\n\n\tif r.instanceSpace[instance].lb == nil {\n\t\tr.instanceSpace[instance].lb = &LeaderBookkeeping{nil, 0, 0, 0, -1, nil, -1}\n\t}\n\n\tr.makeBallot(instance)\n\tr.bcastPrepare(instance)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) executeCommands() {\n\ttimeout := int64(0)\n\tproblemInstance := int32(0)\n\n\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n\t\texecuted := false\n\n\t\t// FIXME idempotence\n\t\tfor i := r.executedUpTo + 1; i <= r.crtInstance; i++ {\n\t\t\tinst := r.instanceSpace[i]\n\t\t\tif inst != nil && inst.cmds != nil && inst.status == COMMITTED {\n\t\t\t\tfor j := 0; j < len(inst.cmds); j++ {\n\t\t\t\t\tif r.Dreply && inst.lb != nil && inst.lb.clientProposals != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tval := inst.cmds[j].Execute(r.State)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpropreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[j].CommandId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tval,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[j].Timestamp}\n\t\t\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(propreply, inst.lb.clientProposals[j].Reply, inst.lb.clientProposals[j].Mutex)\n\t\t\t\t\t} else if inst.cmds[j].Op == state.PUT {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.cmds[j].Execute(r.State)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\texecuted = true\n\t\t\t\tr.executedUpTo++\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tif i == problemInstance {\n\t\t\t\t\ttimeout += SLEEP_TIME_NS\n\t\t\t\t\tif timeout >= COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfor k := problemInstance; k <= r.crtInstance; k++ {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.instancesToRecover <- k\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\tproblemInstance = 0\n\t\t\t\t\t\ttimeout = 0\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tproblemInstance = i\n\t\t\t\t\ttimeout = 0\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif !executed {\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tr.M.Unlock() // FIXME for cache coherence\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(SLEEP_TIME_NS)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb"},{"view_id":"source-view-4","citation_ids":["replica/replica.go:137:577","replica/replica.go:81:136"],"file":"replica/replica.go","start_line":81,"end_line":577,"text":"\n\t\tState:       state.InitState(),\n\t\tRPC:         fastrpc.NewTableId(defs.RPC_TABLE),\n\t\tStableStore: nil,\n\t\tStats:       &defs.Stats{make(map[string]int)},\n\t\tShutdown:    false,\n\t\tListener:    nil,\n\t\tProposeChan: make(chan *defs.GPropose, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\t\tBeaconChan:  make(chan *defs.GBeacon, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n\n\t\tThrifty: thrifty,\n\t\tExec:    exec,\n\t\tLRead:   lread,\n\t\tDreply:  true,\n\t\tBeacon:  false,\n\t\tDurable: false,\n\n\t\tEwma:      make([]float64, n),\n\t\tLatencies: make([]int64, n),\n\n\t\tDt: defs.NewLatencyTable(defs.LatencyConf, defs.IP(), addrs),\n\t}\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < r.N; i++ {\n\t\tr.PreferredPeerOrder[i] = int32((int(r.Id) + 1 + i) % r.N)\n\t\tr.Ewma[i] = 0.0\n\t\tr.Latencies[i] = 0\n\t}\n\n\treturn r\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) Ping(args *defs.PingArgs, reply *defs.PingReply) error {\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) BeTheLeader(args *defs.BeTheLeaderArgs, reply *defs.BeTheLeaderReply) error {\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) FastQuorumSize() int {\n\treturn r.F + (r.F+1)/2\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) SlowQuorumSize() int {\n\treturn (r.N + 1) / 2\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) WriteQuorumSize() int {\n\treturn r.F + 1\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ReadQuorumSize() int {\n\treturn r.N - r.F\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ConnectToPeers() {\n\tvar b [4]byte\n\tbs := b[:4]\n\tdone := make(chan bool)\n\n\tgo r.waitForPeerConnections(done)\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < int(r.Id); i++ {\n\t\tfor {\n\t\t\tif conn, err := net.Dial(\"tcp\", r.PeerAddrList[i]); err == nil {\n\t\t\t\tr.Peers[i] = conn\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(1e9)\n\t\t}\n\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(bs, uint32(r.Id))\n\t\tif _, err := r.Peers[i].Write(bs); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Write id error:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.Alive[i] = true\n\t\tr.PeerReaders[i] = bufio.NewReader(r.Peers[i])\n\t\tr.PeerWriters[i] = bufio.NewWriter(r.Peers[i])\n\t\tr.Printf(\"OUT Connected to %d\", i)\n\t}\n\t<-done\n\tr.Printf(\"Replica %d: done connecting to peers\", r.Id)\n\tr.Printf(\"Node list %v\", r.PeerAddrList)\n\n\tfor rid, reader := range r.PeerReaders {\n\t\tif int32(rid) == r.Id {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tgo r.replicaListener(rid, reader)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ConnectToPeersNoListeners() {\n\tvar b [4]byte\n\tbs := b[:4]\n\tdone := make(chan bool)\n\n\tgo r.waitForPeerConnections(done)\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < int(r.Id); i++ {\n\t\tfor {\n\t\t\tif conn, err := net.Dial(\"tcp\", r.PeerAddrList[i]); err == nil {\n\t\t\t\tr.Peers[i] = conn\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(1e9)\n\t\t}\n\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(bs, uint32(r.Id))\n\t\tif _, err := r.Peers[i].Write(bs); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Write id error:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.Alive[i] = true\n\t\tr.PeerReaders[i] = bufio.NewReader(r.Peers[i])\n\t\tr.PeerWriters[i] = bufio.NewWriter(r.Peers[i])\n\t}\n\t<-done\n\tr.Printf(\"Replica id: %d. Done connecting to peers\\n\", r.Id)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) WaitForClientConnections() {\n\tr.Println(\"Waiting for client connections\")\n\n\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n\t\tconn, err := r.Listener.Accept()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Accept error:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tgo r.clientListener(conn)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) SendMsg(peerId int32, code uint8, msg fastrpc.Serializable) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\tw := r.PeerWriters[peerId]\n\tif w == nil {\n\t\tr.Printf(\"Connection to %d lost!\", peerId)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tw.WriteByte(code)\n\tmsg.Marshal(w)\n\tw.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) SendClientMsg(id int32, code uint8, msg fastrpc.Serializable) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\tw := r.ClientWriters[id]\n\tif w == nil {\n\t\tr.Printf(\"Connection to client %d lost!\", id)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tw.WriteByte(code)\n\tmsg.Marshal(w)\n\tw.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) SendMsgNoFlush(peerId int32, code uint8, msg fastrpc.Serializable) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\tw := r.PeerWriters[peerId]\n\tif w == nil {\n\t\tr.Printf(\"Connection to %d lost!\", peerId)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tw.WriteByte(code)\n\tmsg.Marshal(w)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ReplyProposeTS(reply *defs.ProposeReplyTS, w *bufio.Writer, lock *sync.Mutex) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\treply.Marshal(w)\n\tw.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) SendBeacon(peerId int32) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\tw := r.PeerWriters[peerId]\n\tif w == nil {\n\t\tr.Printf(\"Connection to %d lost!\", peerId)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tw.WriteByte(defs.GENERIC_SMR_BEACON)\n\tbeacon := &defs.Beacon{\n\t\tTimestamp: time.Now().UnixNano(),\n\t}\n\tbeacon.Marshal(w)\n\tw.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ReplyBeacon(beacon *defs.GBeacon) {\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tdefer r.M.Unlock()\n\n\tw := r.PeerWriters[beacon.Rid]\n\tif w == nil {\n\t\tr.Printf(\"Connection to %d lost!\", beacon.Rid)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tw.WriteByte(defs.GENERIC_SMR_BEACON_REPLY)\n\trb := &defs.BeaconReply{\n\t\tTimestamp: beacon.Timestamp,\n\t}\n\trb.Marshal(w)\n\tw.Flush()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) UpdatePreferredPeerOrder(quorum []int32) {\n\taux := make([]int32, r.N)\n\ti := 0\n\tfor _, p := range quorum {\n\t\tif p == r.Id {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\taux[i] = p\n\t\ti++\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, p := range r.PreferredPeerOrder {\n\t\tfound := false\n\t\tfor j := 0; j < i; j++ {\n\t\t\tif aux[j] == p {\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\taux[i] = p\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tr.PreferredPeerOrder = aux\n\tr.M.Unlock()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) ComputeClosestPeers() []float64 {\n\tnpings := 20\n\n\tfor j := 0; j < npings; j++ {\n\t\tfor i := int32(0); i < int32(r.N); i++ {\n\t\t\tif i == r.Id {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tif r.Alive[i] {\n\t\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n\t\t\t\tr.SendBeacon(i)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.Latencies[i] = math.MaxInt64\n\t\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\ttime.Sleep(500 * time.Millisecond)\n\t}\n\n\tquorum := make([]int32, r.N)\n\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tfor i := int32(0); i < int32(r.N); i++ {\n\t\tpos := 0\n\t\tfor j := int32(0); j < int32(r.N); j++ {\n\t\t\tif (r.Latencies[j] < r.Latencies[i]) ||\n\t\t\t\t((r.Latencies[j] == r.Latencies[i]) && (j < i)) {\n\t\t\t\tpos++\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tquorum[pos] = int32(i)\n\t}\n\tr.M.Unlock()\n\n\tif r.Dt == nil {\n\t\tr.UpdatePreferredPeerOrder(quorum)\n\t} else {\n\t\tsort.Slice(r.PreferredPeerOrder, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\t\tdi := r.Dt.WaitDurationID(int(r.PreferredPeerOrder[i]))\n\t\t\tdj := r.Dt.WaitDurationID(int(r.PreferredPeerOrder[j]))\n\t\t\treturn dj == time.Duration(0) || di < dj\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\n\tlatencies := make([]float64, r.N-1)\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < r.N-1; i++ {\n\t\tnode := r.PreferredPeerOrder[i]\n\t\tlat := float64(r.Latencies[node]) / float64(npings*1000000)\n\t\tr.Println(node, \"->\", lat, \"ms\")\n\t\tlatencies[i] = lat\n\t}\n\n\treturn latencies\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) waitForPeerConnections(done chan bool) {\n\tvar b [4]byte\n\tbs := b[:4]\n\n\tport := strings.Split(r.PeerAddrList[r.Id], \":\")[1]\n\tl, err := net.Listen(\"tcp\", \"0.0.0.0:\"+port)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tr.Fatal(r.PeerAddrList[r.Id], err)\n\t}\n\tr.Listener = l\n\tfor i := r.Id + 1; i < int32(r.N); i++ {\n\t\tconn, err := r.Listener.Accept()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Accept error:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, err := io.ReadFull(conn, bs); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Connection establish error:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tid := int32(binary.LittleEndian.Uint32(bs))\n\t\tr.Peers[id] = conn\n\t\tr.PeerReaders[id] = bufio.NewReader(conn)\n\t\tr.PeerWriters[id] = bufio.NewWriter(conn)\n\t\tr.Alive[id] = true\n\t\tr.Printf(\"IN Connected to %d\", id)\n\t}\n\n\tdone <- true\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) replicaListener(rid int, reader *bufio.Reader) {\n\tvar (\n\t\tmsgType      uint8\n\t\terr          error = nil\n\t\tgbeacon      defs.Beacon\n\t\tgbeaconReply defs.BeaconReply\n\t)\n\n\tfor err == nil && !r.Shutdown {\n\t\tif msgType, err = reader.ReadByte(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tswitch uint8(msgType) {\n\n\t\tcase defs.GENERIC_SMR_BEACON:\n\t\t\tif err = gbeacon.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.ReplyBeacon(&defs.GBeacon{\n\t\t\t\tRid:       int32(rid),\n\t\t\t\tTimestamp: gbeacon.Timestamp,\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase defs.GENERIC_SMR_BEACON_REPLY:\n\t\t\tif err = gbeaconReply.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tr.Latencies[rid] += time.Now().UnixNano() - gbeaconReply.Timestamp\n\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n\t\t\tnow := time.Now().UnixNano()\n\t\t\tr.Ewma[rid] = 0.99*r.Ewma[rid] + 0.01*float64(now-gbeaconReply.Timestamp)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tp, exists := r.RPC.Get(msgType)\n\t\t\tif exists {\n\t\t\t\tobj := p.Obj.New()\n\t\t\t\tif err = obj.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tgo func(obj fastrpc.Serializable) {\n\t\t\t\t\ttime.Sleep(r.Dt.WaitDurationID(rid))\n\t\t\t\t\tp.Chan <- obj\n\t\t\t\t}(obj)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.Fatal(\"Error: received unknown message type \", msgType, \" from \", rid)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tr.Alive[rid] = false\n\tr.M.Unlock()\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) clientListener(conn net.Conn) {\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(conn)\n\twriter := bufio.NewWriter(conn)\n\n\tvar (\n\t\tmsgType byte\n\t\terr     error\n\t)\n\n\tr.M.Lock()\n\tr.Println(\"Client up\", conn.RemoteAddr(), \"(\", r.LRead, \")\")\n\tr.M.Unlock()\n\n\taddr := strings.Split(conn.RemoteAddr().String(), \":\")[0]\n\tisProxy := r.Config.Proxy.IsProxy(r.Alias, addr)\n\n\tmutex := &sync.Mutex{}\n\n\tdchan := defs.NewDelayProposeChan(r.Dt.WaitDuration(addr), r.ProposeChan)\n\n\tfor !r.Shutdown && err == nil {\n\t\tif msgType, err = reader.ReadByte(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tswitch uint8(msgType) {\n\t\tcase defs.PROPOSE:\n\t\t\tpropose := &defs.Propose{}\n\t\t\tif err = propose.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tr.ClientWriters[propose.ClientId] = writer\n\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n\t\t\top := propose.Command.Op\n\t\t\tif r.LRead && (op == state.GET || op == state.SCAN) {\n\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(&defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n\t\t\t\t\tOK:        defs.TRUE,\n\t\t\t\t\tCommandId: propose.CommandId,\n\t\t\t\t\tValue:     propose.Command.Execute(r.State),\n\t\t\t\t\tTimestamp: propose.Timestamp,\n\t\t\t\t}, writer, mutex)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tdchan.Write(&defs.GPropose{\n\t\t\t\t\tPropose: propose,\n\t\t\t\t\tReply:   writer,\n\t\t\t\t\tMutex:   mutex,\n\t\t\t\t\tProxy:   isProxy,\n\t\t\t\t\tAddr:    addr,\n\t\t\t\t})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase defs.READ:\n\t\t\t// TODO: do something with this\n\t\t\tread := &defs.Read{}\n\t\t\tif err = read.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase defs.PROPOSE_AND_READ:\n\t\t\t// TODO: do something with this\n\t\t\tpr := &defs.ProposeAndRead{}\n\t\t\tif err = pr.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbreak\n\n\t\tcase defs.STATS:\n\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n\t\t\tb, _ := json.Marshal(r.Stats)\n\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n\t\t\twriter.Write(b)\n\t\t\twriter.Flush()\n\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tp, exists := r.RPC.Get(msgType)\n\t\t\tif exists {\n\t\t\t\tobj := p.Obj.New()\n\t\t\t\tif err = obj.Unmarshal(reader); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tgo func(obj fastrpc.Serializable) {\n\t\t\t\t\ttime.Sleep(r.Dt.WaitDuration(addr))\n\t\t\t\t\tp.Chan <- obj\n\t\t\t\t}(obj)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.Fatal(\"Error: received unknown client message \", msgType)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tconn.Close()\n\tr.Println(\"Client down\", conn.RemoteAddr())\n}\n\nfunc Leader(ballot int32, repNum int) int32 {\n\treturn ballot % int32(repNum)\n}\n\nfunc NextBallotOf(rid, oldBallot int32, repNum int) int32 {\n\treturn (oldBallot/int32(repNum)+1)*int32(repNum) + rid\n}","content_digest":"ea28e2b94198a705e6dd9892a6154ce9b8cb424ec3dedeed8f8bd2488341e766"},{"view_id":"source-view-5","citation_ids":["state/state.go:101:254","state/state.go:1:100"],"file":"state/state.go","start_line":1,"end_line":254,"text":"package state\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/binary\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\n\t\"github.com/emirpasic/gods/maps/treemap\"\n)\n\ntype Operation uint8\n\nconst (\n\tNONE Operation = iota\n\tPUT\n\tGET\n\tSCAN\n)\n\ntype Value []byte\n\nfunc NIL() Value { return Value([]byte{}) }\n\ntype Key int64\n\ntype Command struct {\n\tOp Operation\n\tK  Key\n\tV  Value\n}\n\ntype Id int64\ntype Phase int8\n\nfunc NOOP() []Command { return []Command{{NONE, 0, NIL()}} }\n\ntype State struct {\n\tmutex *sync.Mutex\n\tStore *treemap.Map\n}\n\nfunc KeyComparator(a, b interface{}) int {\n\taAsserted := a.(Key)\n\tbAsserted := b.(Key)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase aAsserted > bAsserted:\n\t\treturn 1\n\tcase aAsserted < bAsserted:\n\t\treturn -1\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc concat(slices []Value) Value {\n\tvar totalLen int\n\tfor _, s := range slices {\n\t\ttotalLen += len(s)\n\t}\n\ttmp := make([]byte, totalLen)\n\tvar i int\n\tfor _, s := range slices {\n\t\ti += copy(tmp[i:], s)\n\t}\n\treturn tmp\n}\n\nfunc InitState() *State {\n\treturn &State{new(sync.Mutex), treemap.NewWith(KeyComparator)}\n}\n\nfunc Conflict(gamma *Command, delta *Command) bool {\n\tkey := gamma.K\n\tlb := delta.K\n\tub := delta.K\n\n\tif gamma.Op == SCAN && delta.Op == SCAN {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\n\tif gamma.Op == SCAN {\n\t\tkey = delta.K\n\t\tlb = gamma.K\n\t\tub = gamma.K + Key(binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(gamma.V))\n\t} else if delta.Op == SCAN {\n\t\tub = delta.K + Key(binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(delta.V))\n\t}\n\n\tif key >= lb && key <= ub {\n\t\tif gamma.Op == PUT || delta.Op == PUT {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc ConflictBatch(batch1 []Command, batch2 []Command) bool {\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(batch1); i++ {\n\t\tfor j := 0; j < len(batch2); j++ {\n\t\t\tif Conflict(&batch1[i], &batch2[j]) {\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc IsRead(command *Command) bool {\n\treturn command.Op == GET\n}\n\nfunc (c *Command) Execute(st *State) Value {\n\n\tst.mutex.Lock()\n\tdefer st.mutex.Unlock()\n\n\tswitch c.Op {\n\tcase PUT:\n\t\tst.Store.Put(c.K, c.V)\n\n\tcase GET:\n\t\tif value, present := st.Store.Get(c.K); present {\n\t\t\tvalAsserted := value.(Value)\n\t\t\treturn valAsserted\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase SCAN:\n\t\tfound := make([]Value, 0)\n\t\tcount := binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(c.V)\n\t\tit := st.Store.Select(func(index interface{}, value interface{}) bool {\n\t\t\tkeyAsserted := index.(Key)\n\t\t\treturn keyAsserted >= c.K && keyAsserted <= c.K+Key(count)\n\t\t}).Iterator()\n\t\tfor it.Next() {\n\t\t\tvalAsserted := it.Value().(Value)\n\t\t\tfound = append(found, valAsserted)\n\t\t}\n\t\tret := concat(found)\n\t\treturn ret\n\t}\n\n\treturn NIL()\n}\n\nfunc (t *Value) String() string {\n\tif t == nil || len(*t) == 0 {\n\t\treturn \"(void)\"\n\t}\n\treturn hex.EncodeToString(*t)\n}\n\nfunc (t *Key) String() string {\n\treturn strconv.FormatInt(int64(*t), 16)\n}\n\nfunc (t *Command) String() string {\n\tret := \"\"\n\tif t.Op == PUT {\n\t\tret = \"PUT( \" + t.K.String() + \" , \" + t.V.String() + \" )\"\n\t} else if t.Op == GET {\n\t\tret = \"GET( \" + t.K.String() + \" )\"\n\t} else if t.Op == SCAN {\n\t\tcount := binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(t.V)\n\t\tret = \"SCAN( \" + t.K.String() + \" , \" + fmt.Sprint(count) + \" )\"\n\t} else {\n\t\tret = \"UNKNOWN( \" + t.V.String() + \" , \" + t.K.String() + \" )\"\n\t}\n\treturn ret\n}\n\nfunc (t *Command) Marshal(w io.Writer) {\n\tt.Op.Marshal(w)\n\tt.K.Marshal(w)\n\tt.V.Marshal(w)\n}\n\nfunc (t *Command) Unmarshal(r io.Reader) error {\n\n\terr := t.Op.Unmarshal(r)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\terr = t.K.Unmarshal(r)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\terr = t.V.Unmarshal(r)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (t *Operation) Marshal(w io.Writer) {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 1)\n\tbs[0] = byte(*t)\n\tw.Write(bs)\n}\n\nfunc (t *Operation) Unmarshal(r io.Reader) error {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 1)\n\tif _, err := io.ReadFull(r, bs); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\t*t = Operation(bs[0])\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (t *Key) Marshal(w io.Writer) {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 8)\n\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint64(bs, uint64(*t))\n\tw.Write(bs)\n}\n\nfunc (t *Key) Unmarshal(r io.Reader) error {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 8)\n\tif _, err := io.ReadFull(r, bs); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\t*t = Key(binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(bs))\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (t *Value) Marshal(w io.Writer) {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 4)\n\tif t == nil {\n\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint16(bs, 0)\n\t\tw.Write(bs)\n\t} else {\n\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint16(bs, uint16(len(*t)))\n\t\tw.Write(bs)\n\t\tw.Write(*t)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (t *Value) Unmarshal(r io.Reader) error {\n\tbs := make([]byte, 4)\n\tif _, err := io.ReadFull(r, bs); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tlen := binary.LittleEndian.Uint16(bs)\n\tbs = make([]byte, len)\n\tif _, err := io.ReadFull(r, bs); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\t*t = Value(bs)\n\treturn nil\n}","content_digest":"58de228aef525681280999221d8cc4d8d14bf7d15b337a5179ce5697d5cba9a5"}],"source_reference_rule":"Material descriptors retain original citation IDs. source_view_id/view_id are text lookup keys, NEVER citation IDs. Cite original material IDs listed in citation_ids, selecting the actual source ranges. Missing text is not permission to infer code."}
